# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal-only files. BOTH GitHub remotes for this project are PUBLIC, so
# anything tracked here is world-readable. These stay on disk but out of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Security audit tracker. Lists the holes that are still OPEN (short JWT_SECRET,
# token in localStorage, no BYO-number ownership proof, call quota off). Publishing
# it hands an attacker a prioritised roadmap. Re-add it only after every item is
# closed, or keep it in a private repo / password manager instead.
docs/SECURITY-REMEDIATION.md

# Pre-launch checklist. Contains real infra identifiers (Vobiz trunk group ID, the
# live DID) plus notes on unfixed weaknesses.
.kiro/steering/pre-launch-checklist.md

# TTS voice-comparison recordings: 5.4 MB of throwaway test audio, regenerated on
# demand. Repo bloat with no product value.
docs/tts-compare/

# Local scratch script that loops through common Postgres passwords

# against localhost. Harmless locally, but a password-guessing loop sitting in a
# public repo looks like an attack tool and adds nothing to the product.
test_db_conn.py
